<InfoPage
  title="Booking Policy"
  description="How reservations work for classes with Handmade Pasta Florence: how to book, confirmation, payment, group sizes, and dietary needs."
  crumbName="Booking Policy"
  lastUpdated="2026-09-03"
>
  <p>This page explains how reservations work for classes run by Handmade Pasta Florence. Please read it before booking. By confirming a class you agree to the terms below.</p>

  <h2>How to book</h2>
  <p>Bookings are made through the "Book a class" button on this site, by WhatsApp at <a href="https://wa.me/393445204379" target="_blank" rel="noopener">+39 344 5204379</a>, or by email at <a href="mailto:ciao@handmadepastaflorence.com">ciao@handmadepastaflorence.com</a>. Tell us the date, the number of guests, and which class you'd like. We reply personally, usually the same day.</p>

  <h2>Confirmation</h2>
  <p>A booking is only confirmed once we've replied by WhatsApp or email confirming your date, time, group size, and price. Sending a request through the site opens the conversation; it doesn't reserve a seat on its own.</p>
  <p>We send the exact kitchen address once your booking is confirmed.</p>

  <h2>Payment</h2>
  <p>A deposit of 30% of the class price is required to lock in your booking. The deposit is paid by bank transfer or by card link (Stripe).</p>
  <p>The remaining balance is paid in cash (EUR) to your chef on the day of the class, or in advance by transfer if you prefer.</p>
  <p>Prices include your host chef, ingredients, and any wine or extras listed on the class page. Personal expenses aren't included unless stated.</p>

  <h2>Group sizes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The Chef's Table: max 8 guests</li>
    <li>Mercato & Mani (market tour + cook): max 6 guests</li>
    <li>The Family Long-Table (private buyout): 6–14 guests</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If you're a smaller or larger group than these, or booking for a corporate event, tell us and we'll suggest the right format.</p>

  <h2>Dietary needs and allergies</h2>
  <p>We can prepare a dedicated gluten-free flour blend and a clean station at no extra charge. This is not a certified gluten-free facility, so let us know about coeliac disease or a serious allergy when you book so we can talk it through with you directly. Please tell us about any other dietary needs or allergies at the same time.</p>

  <h2>Changing or cancelling your booking</h2>
  <p>See our <a href="/cancellation-policy/">Cancellation &amp; Refund</a> page for the full timeline.</p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>Anything not covered here? Write to <a href="mailto:ciao@handmadepastaflorence.com">ciao@handmadepastaflorence.com</a> before you book and we'll give you a clear answer.</p>

  <p class="ip-note">Have a question about how this applies to your booking? Just ask us directly before you book.</p>
</InfoPage>
